        "final_response": "Both findings are addressed. I haven't built or run anything, so none of it is validated.\n\n**`TradeController.trade`** (CCN 11, threshold 10), in `trade-service/.../TradeController.java`:\n- I moved the `userClient.apply` call and its two catch blocks into a private `applyToUser(...)`. It returns the error response, or `null` on success.\n- I moved the RabbitMQ publish and its try/catch into a private `publish(Trade)`.\n- The HTTP statuses, the order of checks and the messages are unchanged.\n\n**`UserController.apply`** (CCN 13, threshold 10), in `user-service/.../UserController.java`:\n- I moved the BUY and SELL branches into private `applyBuy(...)` and `applySell(...)`. Each returns an error message, or `null` on success.\n- `apply` now turns a non-null message into a 400. An unknown type still gives 400 with \"invalid type\".\n- The checks, error messages, cash and position updates, and the `@Transactional` boundary are the same. The helpers are called inside `apply`, so they stay in the same transaction.\n- `applyBuy` uses `u.getId()` where the old code used `uid`. They are the same value, because the user was looked up by `uid`.\n\nNo files outside these two were touched, and the public API, the service topology and the databases are unchanged. Nothing is left unresolved.",
